          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Tired all the time for a couple of months, and my periods have been heavy.",
          "answer": "Feeling tired all the time for a couple of months, along with experiencing heavy periods, could be linked to several conditions. Here are some possibilities based on available information:\n\n1. **Iron-Deficiency Anemia**: This condition can cause fatigue, as well as symptoms like pallor and breathlessness. Heavy menstrual periods can contribute to this anemia, as they may lead to significant blood loss. (Source: General clinical reference on Iron-deficiency anemia)\n\n2. **Hypothyroidism**: An underactive thyroid can lead to fatigue and heavy or irregular menstrual periods. Symptoms often develop gradually and may include weight gain, cold intolerance, and low mood. (Source: General clinical reference on Hypothyroidism)\n\n3. **Other Conditions**: Other factors like chronic fatigue syndrome, diabetes, or even stress and anxiety can lead to fatigue. However, they might not specifically mention heavy periods. \n\nIt is important to discuss these symptoms with a clinician, who can provide a proper evaluation and necessary tests to determine the cause. \n\nWhat I couldn't cover is any specific diagnostic process or treatment plans for these conditions, as well as any other relevant conditions that might contribute to your symptoms.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
